{"id":"code-compare-versions","title":"Semantic version precedence","category":"code","difficulty":4,"prompt":"Write a Python function `compare_versions(a: str, b: str) -> int` that returns -1, 0 or 1\naccording to semantic-version precedence.\n\n- A version is MAJOR.MINOR.PATCH, optionally followed by \"-\" and a pre-release made of\n  dot-separated identifiers, optionally followed by \"+\" and build metadata.\n- MAJOR, MINOR and PATCH compare numerically.\n- A version with a pre-release is lower than the same version without one.\n- Pre-releases compare identifier by identifier: numeric identifiers compare numerically,\n  others compare as ASCII strings, a numeric identifier is lower than a non-numeric one,\n  and if all shared identifiers are equal the shorter pre-release is lower.\n- Build metadata is ignored.","system":"You are completing one task from an evaluation suite. Do the task as asked.\n\nReply with one Python code block that defines exactly what the task asks for. Use only the standard library. Do not include tests, examples, or print statements.","grader":{"type":"code","entrypoint":"compare_versions","tests":["assert compare_versions(\"1.0.0\", \"2.0.0\") == -1","assert compare_versions(\"2.1.0\", \"2.0.9\") == 1","assert compare_versions(\"1.10.0\", \"1.9.0\") == 1","assert compare_versions(\"1.0.0\", \"1.0.0\") == 0","assert compare_versions(\"1.0.0-alpha\", \"1.0.0\") == -1","assert compare_versions(\"1.0.0\", \"1.0.0-rc.1\") == 1","assert compare_versions(\"1.0.0-alpha\", \"1.0.0-alpha.1\") == -1","assert compare_versions(\"1.0.0-alpha.1\", \"1.0.0-alpha.beta\") == -1","assert compare_versions(\"1.0.0-alpha.beta\", \"1.0.0-beta\") == -1","assert compare_versions(\"1.0.0-beta.2\", \"1.0.0-beta.11\") == -1","assert compare_versions(\"1.0.0-beta.11\", \"1.0.0-rc.1\") == -1","assert compare_versions(\"1.0.0+build.5\", \"1.0.0+build.9\") == 0","assert compare_versions(\"1.0.0-beta+exp.sha\", \"1.0.0-beta\") == 0"]},"reference":"```python\ndef compare_versions(a: str, b: str) -> int:\n    def parse(version: str):\n        version = version.split(\"+\", 1)[0]\n        core, _, pre = version.partition(\"-\")\n        numbers = tuple(int(part) for part in core.split(\".\"))\n        return numbers, (pre.split(\".\") if pre else [])\n\n    def cmp(x, y) -> int:\n        return (x > y) - (x < y)\n\n    core_a, pre_a = parse(a)\n    core_b, pre_b = parse(b)\n    if core_a != core_b:\n        return cmp(core_a, core_b)\n    if not pre_a or not pre_b:\n        return cmp(bool(pre_b), bool(pre_a))\n    for x, y in zip(pre_a, pre_b):\n        if x == y:\n            continue\n        if x.isdigit() and y.isdigit():\n            return cmp(int(x), int(y))\n        if x.isdigit() != y.isdigit():\n            return -1 if x.isdigit() else 1\n        return cmp(x, y)\n    return cmp(len(pre_a), len(pre_b))\n```","answers":["```python\ndef compare_versions(a: str, b: str) -> int:\n    def parse(version: str):\n        version = version.split(\"+\", 1)[0]\n        core, _, pre = version.partition(\"-\")\n        return tuple(int(part) for part in core.split(\".\")), pre\n\n    def cmp(x, y) -> int:\n        return (x > y) - (x < y)\n\n    core_a, pre_a = parse(a)\n    core_b, pre_b = parse(b)\n    if core_a != core_b:\n        return cmp(core_a, core_b)\n    if not pre_a or not pre_b:\n        return cmp(bool(pre_b), bool(pre_a))\n    return cmp(pre_a, pre_b)\n```","```python\ndef compare_versions(a: str, b: str) -> int:\n    def parse(version: str):\n        version = version.split(\"+\", 1)[0]\n        core, _, pre = version.partition(\"-\")\n        numbers = tuple(int(part) for part in core.split(\".\"))\n        return numbers, (pre.split(\".\") if pre else [])\n\n    def cmp(x, y) -> int:\n        return (x > y) - (x < y)\n\n    core_a, pre_a = parse(a)\n    core_b, pre_b = parse(b)\n    if core_a != core_b:\n        return cmp(core_a, core_b)\n    if not pre_a or not pre_b:\n        return cmp(bool(pre_b), bool(pre_a))\n    for x, y in zip(pre_a, pre_b):\n        if x == y:\n            continue\n        if x.isdigit() and y.isdigit():\n            return cmp(int(x), int(y))\n        if x.isdigit() != y.isdigit():\n            return -1 if x.isdigit() else 1\n        return cmp(x, y)\n    return cmp(len(pre_a), len(pre_b))\n```"],"cells":[{"arm":"haiku-low","trial":0,"mode":"batch","status":"ok","score":0.92307692,"passed":false,"answer":0,"details":{"passed":12,"total":13,"tests":[{"ok":true},{"ok":true},{"ok":true},{"ok":true},{"ok":true},{"ok":true},{"ok":true},{"ok":true},{"ok":true},{"ok":false,"error":"AssertionError"},{"ok":true},{"ok":true},{"ok":true}],"simulated":{"pass_probability":0.057,"answer":"known-wrong"}},"input_tokens":280,"output_tokens":435,"cost_usd":0.0002455,"latency_ms":null},{"arm":"haiku-low","trial":1,"mode":"batch","status":"ok","score":0.92307692,"passed":false,"answer":0,"details":{"passed":12,"total":13,"tests":[{"ok":true},{"ok":true},{"ok":true},{"ok":true},{"ok":true},{"ok":true},{"ok":true},{"ok":true},{"ok":true},{"ok":false,"error":"AssertionError"},{"ok":true},{"ok":true},{"ok":true}],"simulated":{"pass_probability":0.057,"answer":"known-wrong"}},"input_tokens":280,"output_tokens":377,"cost_usd":0.0002165,"latency_ms":null},{"arm":"haiku-low","trial":2,"mode":"batch","status":"ok","score":0.92307692,"passed":false,"answer":0,"details":{"passed":12,"total":13,"tests":[{"ok":true},{"ok":true},{"ok":true},{"ok":true},{"ok":true},{"ok":true},{"ok":true},{"ok":true},{"ok":true},{"ok":false,"error":"AssertionError"},{"ok":true},{"ok":true},{"ok":true}],"simulated":{"pass_probability":0.057,"answer":"known-wrong"}},"input_tokens":280,"output_tokens":281,"cost_usd":0.0001685,"latency_ms":null},{"arm":"haiku-medium","trial":0,"mode":"batch","status":"ok","score":0.92307692,"passed":false,"answer":0,"details":{"passed":12,"total":13,"tests":[{"ok":true},{"ok":true},{"ok":true},{"ok":true},{"ok":true},{"ok":true},{"ok":true},{"ok":true},{"ok":true},{"ok"